                        "review": "[h3]A wasting heap of terrible mechanics and story barely holding it's head above water[/h3]\n\nThe game does not respect your time, every interactable is highlighted in a bright light sheen and most actions will have you watching a a few second clip of pulling a lever,hitting a button,transforming, ect and the game has no sprint so any backtracking you have to do is spent watching Gabriel take his time with his lil jaunt.\n\nCombat while having plenty of interesting options to use, is full of tedious enemies of little difficulty, that do nothing but drag encounters out turning what should be the best part of the game into an exhausting slog.\n\nThe levels and areas might look nice if everyting wasn't at maximum desaturation 95% of the time, it's grey on grey on slightly dark shade of grey with maybe a little metallic gunmetal mixed in there to form a panel, with the only things bringing colour to the area's being fire or the lights on an interactible.\n\nEnemy design is peak early 2010's with everything being grotesque demons, mutated humans or some guy in a robot, completely abandoning the original Castlevania monster design of having monsters based in mythology or mysticism.\n\nThe bosses are alright at best, and are never really a challange or threat, you are more likely to die from being pushing into a corner by enemies spamming unblockable attacks while being in an unstunable state.\n\nthe stealth sections feel half baked and pointless, mixed in with the ability to turn into a rat makes them longer that they should be.\n\nThe story is abyssmal, it's just straight ass half the time, it's like they had a bunch of guys sitting in a room trying to figure out what would be the darkest story they could write for this game and then just stapled all the ideas together. you will frequently be left scratching your head as characters in the game make the worst awful decisions.\n\nHonestly i quit the game before finishing it because i wasn't enjoying any part of the game. this is the end to a trilogy i feel is better off not existing. only times i ever died was to getting one shot by the golgoth guards which happens when you get caught in any of the stealth sections.\n\nTL:DR the game is an uninspiring and relatively weak action platformer and you are better off playing something else, hopefully something that is actually worth your time and money",
